  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Saturday/... Wednesday will see the\ntail end of an active weather pattern from a low pressure system\nin the gulf, with rain and wind diminishing through the day. This\nlow is expected to move south out of the area through the \nday Thursday, which looks to be a period of drier conditions and \ncalmer winds. The upper level flow looks to shift to be more \nsoutherly, but not fully offshore, so the southern panhandle, \nespecially, could see more showery conditions. Late Friday or \novernight into Saturday, another front looks to move across the \npanhandle, bringing elevated winds back to the inner channels, up\nto about 20-25kts, with periods of heavier rain. This system is \nnot expected to bring unseasonable amounts of rain, so there is no\nmajor flooding concern at this time.",
